  "probe": "r-oledb-odbc/prop-command-set-execute",
  "bookRefs": [
    "R-OLEDB-1",
    "OLE-PROP",
    "OLE-FETCH"
  ],
  "description": "OLE-PROP requests through a Command: read the Command.Properties inventory before execution; then, in order, set Maximum Rows = 5, 0 and 100, Bookmarkable = True, Hold Rows = True, Others' Changes Visible = True, Updatability = 7, Immobile Rows = True, Literal Bookmarks = True and the unknown name Jet OLEDB:Nonexistent through the retained collection, reading Attributes and the value back, and after each Execute of 'SELECT ID, V FROM Seq ORDER BY ID' read State, cursor settings, RecordCount, the Supports of adBookmark and every row. Asks which settable properties the Command accepts, which change the result and how many rows are fetched.",
  "callerSurface": "native-idispatch/x64",
  "invokeLcid": 1033,
  "observationRecipe": [
    "clearErrorInfoBefore",
